Faraday Industrial Benchmark
Copyright 2026 Faraday Industrial Benchmark contributors

The Faraday-native implementation and authored benchmark content are original
synthetic work. Separately namespaced, pinned snapshots of permissively licensed
public benchmarks are distributed under third_party/upstreams for compatibility
and comparative evaluation. They are not Faraday-authored content and are not
part of the Faraday-native headline score.

This distribution includes software developed by Blobfish AI, the Industrial
Agent Benchmark project, the SupChain-Bench project, and IBM's AssetOpsBench
contributors. Their original license and notice files are preserved in each
snapshot. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and third_party/manifest.json.

The distributor operations families (data/distributor-*, data/distributor-sources,
and src/faraday_industrial_benchmark/distributor) are native Faraday rebuilds of
tasks selected from three public benchmarks. Their fixtures are derived from
pinned upstream snapshots, and each source keeps a provenance record with
SHA-256 hashes under data/distributor-sources/<source>/provenance.json:

- ERP-Bench by Agentic Labs (CC0-1.0).
- ERPBench-100 by Blobfish AI (code Apache-2.0, data CC BY 4.0). Changes were
  made: tasks were converted into Faraday scenarios, tools, and criteria.
- GDPval by OpenAI. The dataset card declares no license. Its expected
  deliverables and rubrics are included only as grader-only reference material
  for the GDPval-derived tasks. They are not relicensed by Faraday, are not
  covered by DATA_LICENSE, and remain subject to OpenAI's terms. They will be
  removed on request from the rights holder.

No customer data, proprietary vendor UI, private benchmark split, or restricted
question bank is included.
